# gitleaks fingerprint allowlist — supplementary to .gitleaks.toml.
# Format: one "<commit>:<file>:<rule-id>:<line>" per line.
#
# Path-based allowlist in .gitleaks.toml is the primary mechanism
# (commit-invariant); this file pins specific historical findings
# whose path-based form would also catch legitimate future scans.
#
# NB: the comment in this file MUST NOT quote any text from the
# scanned source file, because gitleaks scans the ignore file too
# and any quoted trigger text would itself become a finding.

# Historical finding from step 15 commit (.gitleaksignore line 6 at
# commit 66368cd). The step-15 commit message and the original
# .gitleaksignore comment contained a glossary fragment that the
# generic-api-key heuristic flags as high-entropy. The current
# file no longer contains the trigger, but git history retains it
# and a full-history scan (`gitleaks detect --source .`) will see it.
66368cd41218406cfde0cc95464b196f28ec38ed:.gitleaksignore:generic-api-key:6
